35,2,1,talk,May,,"The pilots actually worked. No faults, costs covered. But ticketing fees are eating our paving budget. That is a red flag.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,The late-turn pool is hollow. Overtime is masking a structural gap. We cannot promise schedules we cannot staff.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Midori,,"The audits show waiting for connections is the real time sink, not ticket queues. The accessibility records show lifts finished, but lane priorities failed.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shizue,,The committee minutes show ferry and rail data terms are still unresolved. The pre-war shells hide voids that stop work for weeks.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
